-- title:
--   Reciprocal annulus pair at a crossing-model node
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$ which is a curve over $L$ (principal divisors exist, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$) and of essentially finite type. Let $R_1,R_2$ be regular prolongations of $A$ to $F$ with residue maps onto fields $\bar F_1,\bar F_2$ over the residue field of $A$, and let $x_1,x_2$ be places of $\bar F_1,\bar F_2$ over that residue field, both rational. Let $S$ be a set of places of $F/L$, all rational, and $\mathcal N\subseteq F$ the subring consisting of the $f$ lying in $R_1$'s and $R_2$'s valuation rings and in the valuation ring of every $P\in S$; it is assumed that $P(f)\in A$ for $f\in\mathcal N$ and $P\in S$, that the two residues of such an $f$ have non-negative order at $x_1$, resp. $x_2$, when non-zero, and that whenever both residues of an $f$ are non-zero the set of $P\in S$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P f\neq 0$ is finite and $\sum_{P\in S}\operatorname{ord}_P f=\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}\bar f^{(1)}+\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}\bar f^{(2)}$. Let $\mathcal N_0\le\mathcal N$ be a Noetherian local subring such that $S$ is exactly the set of places whose valuation ring contains $\mathcal N_0$ and which send every non-unit of $\mathcal N_0$ into the maximal ideal of $A$, and such that every $f\in F$ satisfies $fb=\sum_i c_i a_i$ with $c_i\in L$, $a_i\in\mathcal N_0$ and $0\neq b\in\mathcal N_0$. Let $C\subseteq A$ be a subring mapping into $\mathcal N_0$, a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with $\varpi\in C$ non-zero such that the residue map of $A$ kills exactly $\varpi C$, every element of $A$ algebraic over $C$, every element of $\mathcal N_0$ congruent to a constant from $C$ modulo non-units; assume also that for $a,b\in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b\neq0$ one has $b\mid a^n$ for some $n$. Finally let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring with irreducible $\pi$, let $E\ge 1$, let $\sigma:W\to\widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ (adic completion at the maximal ideal) send $\pi$ to the image of $\varpi$, and let $\iota:\widehat{\mathcal N_0}\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{E})$ be a ring isomorphism carrying $\sigma$ to `const (π ^ E)`, subject to the two regularity laws: for $f\in\mathcal N_0$ whose residue at $R_1$ is non-zero of order $n$ at $x_1$, $\iota(f)$ equals a unit times `V (π ^ E) ^ n` modulo the ideal generated by `const (π ^ E) π` and `U (π ^ E)`, and symmetrically with $R_2$, $x_2$, `U` and `V` interchanged. Let $x,y\in\mathcal N_0$ with the residue of $x$ at $R_1$ zero and $\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}$ of its residue at $R_2$ equal to $1$, the residue of $y$ at $R_2$ zero and $\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}$ of its residue at $R_1$ equal to $1$, and $xy=\varpi^{E_0}u$ with $u$ a unit of $\mathcal N_0$. Then there are two annuli $An,An'$ over $A$ in $F$ (each given by a set of places, a parameter and a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, satisfying the annulus axioms: rationality and integrality of the parameter at each place of the domain, the parameter's value in the maximal ideal and non-zero with the modulus divisible by it, unique realisation of each admissible value, $\operatorname{ord}_P(\text{param}-P(\text{param}))=1$, and the unit principle) with: $An.\mathrm{dom}=S$ as sets of places, $An'.\mathrm{dom}=An.\mathrm{dom}$ and $An'.\mathrm{modulus}=An.\mathrm{modulus}$, the modulus equal to $\varpi^{E_0}$ in $L$ and non-zero, $An.\mathrm{param}=y$, $An'.\mathrm{param}\cdot An.\mathrm{param}$ the image of the modulus in $F$, and both ends attached: $An.\mathrm{param}$ lies in $R_1$'s valuation ring with residue of order $1$ at $x_1$, and for every $f$ in that ring with non-zero residue and $\operatorname{ord}_P f=0$ for all $P\in An.\mathrm{dom}$, the element $P(f)\cdot P(An.\mathrm{param})^{-\operatorname{ord}_{x_1}\bar f}$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there for every such $P$; symmetrically for $An'$, $R_2$ and $x_2$.
--
--   This is the node half of the construction of semistable charts on a curve read through its function field: from a presentation of the completed local ring of the node as the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$ it produces the pair of mutually reciprocal annuli, of modulus $\varpi^{E_0}$, on the two branches, each attached to the corresponding component chart by the unit statement for functions with no zeros or poles on the annulus. It is obtained from the node annulus engine ([`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.exists_mem_and_evalAt_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.exists_mem_and_evalAt_eq), [`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.eq_of_mem_of_evalAt_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.eq_of_mem_of_evalAt_eq), [`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.ord_sub_evalAt_eq_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.ord_sub_evalAt_eq_one)) and feeds the full-level modular curve statements assembling tube annuli, discs, node rings and node charts.
